@model Portal.Pages.RuntimeModel
@{
    var consequence = Model.Consequence;
}
@*  Swap target 4 of 4: the one sentence that belongs to the path rather than to any single stage,
    so it spans the whole deck.

    It composes across every stage and therefore re-reads all of them — each through the response
    cache, so this costs no Azure call.

    Two things about it that must survive a redesign:

    - It renders on a quiet day. A bar that disappears when nothing is wrong trains an operator not
      to look at it, and this bar is the accessible carrier of the schematic's whole thesis: the
      ducts are CSS decoration and are invisible to assistive technology, so the relationship they
      draw exists in the accessibility tree only as this sentence (design.md D3).
    - When a source is unread it says so, and states neither that the fleet is constrained nor that
      it is not. The console does not guess on Resource Manager's behalf. *@
<div hx-get="/Runtime?handler=Consequence" hx-trigger="every 60s" hx-swap="outerHTML"
     style="display:contents">
    <div class="sx-conseq @consequence.Tone">
        <span class="bico" aria-hidden="true">@consequence.Icon</span>
        <span><strong>@consequence.Headline</strong> @consequence.Detail</span>
    </div>
</div>
